  "answer": "Semiguided dialogue refers to a dialogue structure where the conversation is partially controlled through a system that offers multiple suitable and relevant state transitions to the participants, guiding the interaction while still allowing for some flexibility. The guided part of the dialogue is the structured transitions and options provided to the Wizard, which help in navigating the conversation effectively [E2][E5].",
